 * one line per component of each rule's `<rule>__rhs` signature -- the result and each parameter --
 * with whether the type table holds that component (`interned=yes|no|absent`).
 *
 * The right side of a rule here is a function value (`x + w => (dx: float, dw: float) => dx`), so
 * the signature's result type is a closure type, and a closure type built on a path that interns
 * only itself leaves its own result out of the table: `typeId() == 0`. The plan asserts that every
 * component of every `__rhs` signature is in the table, one component at a time.
 */
